[ ] Archive session files from every host to the server =session-archive $Owner-built. Systemd user timer per host (dabdesktop, home server) running rsync -a without --delete over Tailscale SSH into raw/<host>/<harness>/ on the server; cover every Linux user and headless (claude -p, cron) session location; loginctl enable-linger on the server; archive mode 700. Acceptance: sessions older than cleanupPeriodDays survive in the archive.$ !1 +infrastructure ^2026-09-22T23:11 #01a0cce3-e325-7290-a73a-4262e5038865
[ ] Explore raw session records before designing a schema =session-explore $Owner-led. Point DuckDB read_json_auto at the Claude Code archive and look at what records actually contain; bring back the most surprising findings and choose the first question (default: overnight-run morning summary). Acceptance: a written first question and the fields it needs.$ !2 +evaluation ^2026-09-22T23:11 <session-archive #01a0cce3-e343-7c42-8dd4-8cb3dd34718c
[ ] Capture per-harness payload fixtures =harness-fixtures $Save real Claude Code Read hook payloads and Pi read results with their expected observe-read inputs; test capture-read.py and the Pi extension against them. The archive normalizers reuse the same fixtures. Acceptance: a format change fails a test instead of silently dropping captures.$ !2 +testing ^2026-09-22T23:11 #01a0cce3-e36b-74f0-b2da-f0d9f8fc88bd
[ ] Stamp harness session identity on workspace events =session-identity $Proposed; needs owner confirmation as a kernel change. Carry (host, harness, session_id) on observation and write events so they can be joined with the archive. Acceptance: executable coverage showing identity recorded from both the Claude Code hook and the Pi extension.$ !3 +architecture ^2026-09-22T23:11 #01a0cce3-e399-7352-8780-fdc8c0afa544
[ ] Measure read-capture rate from the archive =capture-rate $First cross-source query: reconcile archived Read calls against kernel observations to get the capture rate and reasons for misses, which the fail-silent hook currently hides. Acceptance: a reproducible query and a field report under knowledge/evaluations/.$ !3 +evaluation ^2026-09-22T23:11 <session-explore <session-identity #01a0cce3-e3c2-7112-82a8-4229ef788a6d
